        ],
        "statement": "Let $(S,m)$ be a finite Coxeter matrix, $W$ the presented group with length $\\ell$, $V=\\mathbb R^S$ with Coxeter form $B$, the canonical reflection homomorphism $\\rho$, the signed root system $\\Phi=\\Phi_+\\sqcup\\Phi_-$, the positive cone $V_+=\\{\\sum_s\\lambda_se_s:\\lambda_s\\ge0\\}$ and the reflection set $T$ ([[def-cg-real-coxeter-form-and-reflection]], [[def-cg-canonical-reflection-homomorphism]], [[thm-cg-root-sign-and-simple-reflection-positivity]]), with inversion sets $N(w)$ ([[def-cg-geometric-inversion-set]]) and descent sets $D_L,D_R$ ([[def-cg-parabolic-quotient-and-two-sided-minima]] (2)).\n\n**(1) Full left descent forces finiteness.** Suppose $x\\in W$ satisfies $D_L(x)=S$, i.e. $\\ell(sx)<\\ell(x)$ for every $s\\in S$. Then:\n(i) $\\rho(x^{-1})\\Phi_+=\\Phi_-$ and $N(x^{-1})=\\Phi_+$;\n(ii) $\\Phi$ is finite, $|\\Phi_+|=\\ell(x)=|T|$, and $W$ is finite;\n(iii) $x$ is the longest element $w_0$ of $W$; equivalently $x$ is the unique element of $W$ with $N(x^{-1})=\\Phi_+$; and $x^{-1}=x$ as well as $\\ell(w_0w)=\\ell(w_0)-\\ell(w)$ for all $w\\in W$.\n\n**(2) Parabolic form.** Let $J\\subseteq S$, let $W_J=\\langle s:s\\in J\\rangle$ be the standard parabolic subgroup, $V_J=\\mathrm{span}\\{e_s:s\\in J\\}$, $\\Phi_J=\\Phi\\cap V_J=\\Phi_J^+\\sqcup\\Phi_J^-$ the parabolic root subsystem of [[thm-cg-parabolic-intersections-and-coset-factorization]] (2), and put $N_J(y):=\\{\\alpha\\in\\Phi_J^+:\\rho(y)\\alpha\\in\\Phi_J^-\\}$ for $y\\in W_J$. If $w\\in W_J$ satisfies $\\ell(sw)<\\ell(w)$ for every $s\\in J$, then $W_J$ is finite, $N_J(w^{-1})=\\Phi_J^+$, and $w=w_0(J)$ is the longest element of the Coxeter system $(W_J,J)$. No Choice is used.",
        "strategy": "(1) From D_L(x)=S, the descent/root dictionary sends every simple root under rho(x^{-1}) into Phi_-. Every positive root is a nonzero nonnegative combination of simple roots, so linearity sends it into -V_+; since rho(x^{-1}) permutes Phi and the image is nonzero, it lies in Phi_-. Thus N(x^{-1})=Phi_+. Inversion counts give |Phi_+|=ell(x), the root-reflection dictionary gives finite Phi and finite T, and faithfulness embeds W in Sym(Phi). The finite-parabolic-longest supplier then identifies x with the unique w0 and supplies its length and involution properties. (2) For J⊆S, parabolic invariance gives rho(W_J)V_J=V_J. Restrict the canonical representation to V_J; its simple-generator maps are the reflections for the restricted Coxeter form, so the restricted and subsystem canonical maps agree by the presentation universal property. Apply the root-sign argument inside V_J to show N_J(w^{-1})=Phi_J^+; the inversion formula and intrinsic-length identity make Phi_J finite, faithfulness makes W_J finite, and clause (1) applied to (W_J,J) identifies w=w0(J). No Bruhat lifting or Choice is used.",
