          "source": "def-cg-parabolic-quotient-and-two-sided-minima",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "**(2) Descents and the one-sided quotients.** For $w\\in W$ put\n\n$$D_L(w):=\\{s\\in S:\\ell(sw)<\\ell(w)\\},\\qquad D_R(w):=\\{s\\in S:\\ell(ws)<\\ell(w)\\};$$\n\neach of $\\ell(sw)-\\ell(w)$ and $\\ell(ws)-\\ell(w)$ lies in $\\{\\pm1\\}$\n([[thm-hh-coxeter-exchange-deletion-and-faithfulness]] (1)). Define\n\n$$W^I:=\\{w\\in W:\\ell(ws)>\\ell(w)\\text{ for all }s\\in I\\}=\\{w\\in W:D_R(w)\\cap I=\\emptyset\\},$$\n\n$${}^IW:=\\{w\\in W:\\ell(sw)>\\ell(w)\\text{ for all }s\\in I\\}=\\{w\\in W:D_L(w)\\cap I=\\emptyset\\}.$$\n\nConventions are fixed here: in ${}^IW$ the subset $I$ is tested on the left, in\n$W^I$ it is tested on the right; $\\ell(sw)$ means left multiplication by $s$\nand $\\ell(ws)$ right multiplication. The interpretation of these sets as sets\nof coset representatives is not part of the definition; it is quoted from\n[[thm-hh-parabolic-minimal-representatives-and-length-additivity]] (3) and\nre-examined in [[thm-cg-parabolic-intersections-and-coset-factorization]] (3):\nevery $w\\in W$ has a unique factorization\n\n$$w=u\\,d\\qquad(u\\in W_I,\\ d\\in{}^IW),\\qquad \\ell(w)=\\ell(u)+\\ell(d),$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the unique element of minimal length in the left coset $W_Iw$, and\nit satisfies $\\ell(ud)=\\ell(u)+\\ell(d)$ for all $u\\in W_I$; symmetrically every\n$w\\in W$ has a unique factorization\n\n$$w=d\\,v\\qquad(d\\in W^I,\\ v\\in W_I),\\qquad \\ell(w)=\\ell(d)+\\ell(v),$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the unique element of minimal length in the right coset $wW_I$, and\nit satisfies $\\ell(dv)=\\ell(d)+\\ell(v)$ for all $v\\in W_I$. Thus ${}^IW$\nconsists exactly of the elements of minimal length in the left cosets\n$W_Iw=\\{uw:u\\in W_I\\}$ and $W^I$ consists exactly of the elements of minimal\nlength in the sets $wW_I=\\{wv:v\\in W_I\\}$. Inversion gives\n$W^I=({}^IW)^{-1}$, because $\\ell(x)=\\ell(x^{-1})$ and $(sw)^{-1}=w^{-1}s$.",
