        {
          "fact": "F10",
          "source": "thm-hh-parabolic-minimal-representatives-and-length-additivity",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "2. **Intrinsic parabolic presentation.** Let $W_J^\\ast$ be the group presented by the restricted Coxeter matrix $(J,m|_J)$ in the sense of [[def-hh-coxeter-matrix-word-group-and-length]]. The canonical homomorphism $W_J^\\ast\\to W_J$, $s\\mapsto s$, is an isomorphism. Hence $(W_J,J)$ is a Coxeter system, its intrinsic length function $\\ell_J$ agrees with the ambient length $\\ell$ on $W_J$, and $W_J\\cap S=J$.",
          "uses": [
            "5.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F11",
          "source": "thm-cg-finite-parabolic-longest-element-and-opposition",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "**(1) The opposition and the longest element of a finite Coxeter system.** Suppose $W$ is\nfinite. Then:\n\n(i) there is a unique $w_0\\in W$ with $w_0\\cdot C=-C$; equivalently $w_0$ is the unique\nelement of $W$ with $N(w_0)=\\Phi_+$ (equivalently with $N(w_0^{-1})=\\Phi_+$);\n\n(ii) $\\ell(w_0)=|N(w_0)|=|\\Phi_+|=|T|$, and $\\rho(w_0)\\Phi_+=\\Phi_-$;\n\n(iii) $\\ell(w_0w)=\\ell(w_0)-\\ell(w)$ and $\\ell(ww_0)=\\ell(w_0)-\\ell(w)$ for every $w\\in W$;\nconsequently $\\ell(w_0)=\\max\\{\\ell(w):w\\in W\\}$ and $w_0$ is the unique element of that\nlength (the element of longest length);\n\n(iv) $w_0^2=1$;\n\n(v) $w_0Sw_0^{-1}=S$, and there is a permutation $\\sigma$ of $S$ with\n$\\rho(w_0)e_s=-e_{\\sigma(s)}$, equivalently $w_0sw_0=\\sigma(s)$, for every $s\\in S$.",
          "uses": [
            "4.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F12",
          "source": "def-cg-real-coxeter-form-and-reflection",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "**(2) The Coxeter form.** For finite $m(s,t)$ put $c(s,t):=\\cos(\\pi/m(s,t))$ ([[def-sine-and-cosine-by-power-series]], [[def-pi-via-first-positive-cosine-zero]]) and for $m(s,t)=\\infty$ put $c(s,t):=1$; then $c(s,t)=c(t,s)$ and $c(s,s)=\\cos\\pi=-1$. The **Coxeter form** $B$ is the unique symmetric bilinear form on $V$ with $B(e_s,e_t)=-c(s,t)$ for all $s,t\\in S$; in particular $B(e_s,e_s)=1$ and $B(e_s,e_t)=-\\cos(\\pi/m(s,t))$ for finite $m(s,t)$, while $B(e_s,e_t)=-1$ when $m(s,t)=\\infty$ ([[def-bilinear-symmetric-skew-and-alternating-forms]], [[thm-bilinear-forms-correspond-to-linear-maps-into-the-dual]]). **No positive definiteness, definiteness or nondegeneracy of $B$ is presumed**: $\\operatorname{rad}(B):=\\{u:B(u,v)=0\\text{ for all }v\\in V\\}$ may be nonzero ([[def-matrix-radicals-rank-and-nondegeneracy-of-a-bilinear-form]]), and the form may be indefinite ([[def-definiteness-inertia-and-signature-data-over-the-reals]]). A linear map $g:V\\to V$ is **$B$-preserving** when $B(gu,gw)=B(u,w)$ for all $u,w\\in V$.",
          "uses": [
            "5.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F13",
          "source": "def-cg-real-coxeter-form-and-reflection",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "**(3) Reflections.** For $a\\in V$ with $B(a,a)\\ne0$ define the **reflection with normal $a$** by $$r_a(v):=v-\\frac{2B(v,a)}{B(a,a)}a .$$ The definition asserts neither that $r_a$ is linear or an involution nor that $\\ker B(-,a)=\\{v:B(v,a)=0\\}$ is a hyperplane; these are proved in [[lem-cg-reflection-form-invariance-and-rank-two-orders]]. When $B(a,a)=0$ the symbol $r_a$ is not defined.",
          "uses": [
            "5.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F14",
          "source": "def-hh-coxeter-matrix-word-group-and-length",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "**Universal property.** For every group $G$ and every map $f:S\\to G$ with $f(s)^2=1$ for all $s\\in S$ and $(f(s)f(t))^{m(s,t)}=1$ in $G$ for all $s\\ne t$ with $m(s,t)<\\infty$, there is a unique group homomorphism $\\varphi:W\\to G$ with $\\varphi(s)=f(s)$ for all $s\\in S$ ([[def-group-homomorphism]], [[thm-quotient-group-universal-property]], [[thm-von-dyck]], [[def-group-presentation]], [[def-relators-relations-and-finite-presentations]], [[prop-equality-of-words-in-a-presentation]]).",
          "uses": [
            "5.1"
          ]
        },
